<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sant'Apollinare Nuovo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sant'Apollinare Nuovo is a basilica in Ravenna built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric the Great</a> in the early 6th century as his Arian palace church. Its nave mosaics show processions of martyrs and virgins, scenes from the life of Christ and a view of Theodoric's palace, from which figures of the Gothic court were later removed. It is part of a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santapollinare-nuovo.jpg" alt="Sant'Apollinare Nuovo" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ravenna,_sant%27apollinare_nuovo,_ext._01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
